From 1d608df5319d4fd0db8c6a8da25fb602fde4d29a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:39:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] video: fb window - aspect-fit any frame size, fullscreen,
 DPI, GPU present hooks

The framebuffer window scales the frame to its client area keeping the
aspect, with black bars, and takes frames of any size from
xbox_FramebufferWindowPresentPixels (they used to be cropped to 640x480).
Alt+Enter toggles borderless fullscreen on the window's monitor (not passed
on as a key press); RECOMP_FB_FULLSCREEN=1 starts that way. WM_SIZE,
WM_PAINT and WM_DPICHANGED are handled, and the window thread is per-monitor
DPI aware while the process stays unaware.

For a renderer that draws into the window itself (a GL context on its DC):
xbox_FramebufferWindowHwnd(), xbox_FramebufferWindowGpuPresent(1) to stop
the GDI blit, and xbox_FramebufferWindowClientSize() in physical pixels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ahYm8JBvCH5KhgtSu9Yoy
